      "year": 2023,
      "revenue_cr": 203151,
      "net_income_cr": 37609,
      "eps": 68.07
    },
    {
      "year": 2024,
      "revenue_cr": 239051,
      "net_income_cr": 41340,
      "eps": 74.84
    }
  ],
  "reasoning": "Consolidated revenues (Income from Operations) were 147068 crore in FY2020 and 155885 crore in FY2021 (Domestic 154953 + International 932), yielding a revenue growth rate of approximately 17.6% YoY; consolidated net income grew from 27296 crore in FY2020 to 31117 crore in FY2021, a growth rate of approximately 14.0% YoY. These FY2021 growth rates (17.6% for revenue, 14.0% for net income) are applied consistently to project FY2022\u2013FY2024 figures. EPS is calculated using the FY2021 diluted weighted average share count of approximately 552.54 crore shares held constant across the forecast period."
}

Step 1: Identify the 3 most critical assumptions embedded in this forecast.
Step 2: For each assumption, describe one plausible scenario where it fails.
Step 3: Rate each assumption failure as Low / Medium / High risk to the forecast accuracy.
Step 4: Assign an overall confidence score from 0-100 (100 = completely certain).

